# Neo Multiband parameters (docs/specs/machines.md §5). The order is permanent: songs and presets
# store values by position. Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoMultiband
namespace NeoBuzz.Multiband
class NeoMultibandMachine
summary Multiband compressor and upward expander for mastering and buses: 3 or 4 bands split by linear-phase crossovers (the bands sum back to the input exactly; about 96 ms of latency, reported to NeoBuzz Live) or zero-latency minimum-phase ones (Linkwitz–Riley, the same band shapes), each band with threshold, ratio (above 1:1 compresses, below 1:1 expands upward), attack, release, knee, range, makeup, solo and bypass; the detector (peak or RMS) linked in stereo or in mid/side; per band upward compression below the threshold and an external sidechain (input 2); lookahead; a Dynamic phase mode (zero latency, the input as the dry); mix and output. With every band at 1:1 and 0 dB it passes the input, delayed by the latency, bit for bit. Use it to control the lows, tame harshness, de-ess, glue a bus or lift the air of a master.

group Crossovers
Bands     "Bands"        0 1     1     enum 3_bands 4_bands          | Three bands (Crossover 1 and 2) or four (all three crossovers)
    how Chooses three or four bands for the dynamics.
    sound Four bands give finer control over the top end; three keep things simpler.
Xo1       "Crossover 1"  0 10000 2594  freq 20 20000                 | Between bands 1 and 2 (Linkwitz–Riley, 24 dB/oct, −6 dB here)
    how Sets the frequency between bands 1 and 2, from 20 Hz to 20 kHz.
    sound It decides how much of the low end belongs to the lowest band.
Xo2       "Crossover 2"  0 10000 5663  freq 20 20000                 | Between bands 2 and 3 (never below Crossover 1)
    how Sets the frequency between bands 2 and 3.
    sound It moves the boundary between the lower and upper midrange.
Xo3       "Crossover 3"  0 10000 8257  freq 20 20000                 | Between bands 3 and 4 with four bands (never below Crossover 2)
    how Sets the frequency between bands 3 and 4 when four bands are used.
    sound It decides where the top band begins.
Phase     "Phase"        0 2     0     enum Linear Minimum Dynamic   | Linear: the bands sum back to the input exactly, no phase shift, about 96 ms of latency (reported to NeoBuzz Live). Minimum: zero latency, the same band shapes, the crossovers' phase shift (as an analog crossover's). Dynamic: zero latency and no static phase shift: the output is the input plus each band's gain change times the band, so a band at 0 dB change leaves the input exactly as it was (the crossovers' phase shift shows only where a band is changing)
    how Chooses Linear (about 96 ms latency, no phase shift), Minimum (no latency, crossover phase shift) or Dynamic (no latency, phase shift only where a band changes).
    sound Linear and Dynamic keep the untouched sound exactly as it was, which suits mastering; Minimum suits live use where latency matters.
group Detector
Stereo    "Stereo"       0 1     0     enum L/R M/S                  | What each band's detector and gain work on: left and right, or mid and side
    how Chooses whether the bands work on left and right, or on mid and side.
    sound Mid/side lets the centre and the width be compressed separately.
Link      "Link"         0 1000  1000  pct                           | 100 %: both channels (or mid and side) get the same gain, from the louder; 0 %: each its own
    how Sets how much both channels share the same gain, from 0 % to 100 %.
    sound Linked keeps the stereo image steady; unlinked lets each side react on its own.
group Band 1
B1Threshold "B1 threshold" 0 600 400 lin -60 0 dB 1 | Band 1: level where the gain starts to change (the band's peak)
    how Sets the level, from -60 to 0 dB, at which band 1's gain starts to change.
    sound Lower values act on more of the band and make it denser and more even.
B1Ratio "B1 ratio" 0 1200 400 ratio 0.5 32 inf | Band 1: above 1:1 compresses above the threshold (∞: limits); below 1:1 expands upward (0.5:1 doubles the level over the threshold); 1:1 does nothing
    how Sets band 1's ratio: above 1:1 it compresses, below 1:1 it expands, and 1:1 does nothing.
    sound Higher ratios squeeze the band harder; ratios under 1:1 make loud parts louder.
B1Attack "B1 attack" 0 1000 722 time 0.00005 0.2 | Band 1: time to 63 % of a gain change
    how Sets how fast band 1's gain reacts, from 0.05 ms to 200 ms.
    sound Fast attacks tame the start of hits; slow ones let them through for more punch.
B1Release "B1 release" 0 1000 612 time 0.005 3 | Band 1: time back to 37 % of a gain change
    how Sets how fast band 1's gain returns, from 5 ms to 3 s.
    sound Short releases sound lively and can pump; long ones sound smooth.
B1Knee "B1 knee" 0 240 60 lin 0 24 dB 1 | Band 1: width of the soft knee around the threshold
    how Sets how gradually band 1's dynamics start around the threshold, from 0 to 24 dB.
    sound Wider knees are smoother and less noticeable.
B1Range "B1 range" 0 240 240 lin 0 24 dB 1 | Band 1: the most the gain changes, either way
    how Limits how far band 1's gain can change either way, from 0 to 24 dB.
    sound A small range keeps the effect gentle; a large one allows strong action.
B1Makeup "B1 makeup" 0 480 240 lin -24 24 dB 1 | Band 1: gain after the dynamics (negative cuts the band)
    how Adds or removes up to 24 dB of gain on band 1 after the dynamics.
    sound Positive values lift the band; negative values cut it, changing the tonal balance.
B1Solo "B1 solo" 0 1 0 switch | Band 1: hear only the soloed bands (processed, Mix ignored)
    how Plays only the soloed bands, processed, ignoring Mix.
    sound You hear band 1 by itself, which helps you set its dynamics.
B1Bypass "B1 bypass" 0 1 0 switch | Band 1: pass the band untouched (no dynamics, no makeup)
    how Passes band 1 untouched, with no dynamics and no makeup.
    sound Band 1 sounds as it came in, so you can compare with and without it.
