group Output
Mix       "Mix"          0 1000  1000  pct                           | Dry against the processed bands (the dry is latency-aligned, so parallel compression never combs)
    how Blends the dry signal with the processed bands.
    sound Lower values add the dynamics as a parallel layer, keeping punch and detail.
Output    "Output"       0 480   240   db -24 24                     | Output gain, −24 … +24 dB in 0.1 dB steps
    how Sets the output gain, from -24 to +24 dB.
    sound It makes the whole sound louder or quieter without changing the tone.

# Added in M6b (docs/specs/mastering-tools.md §5.14): appended, so songs and presets keep their values; at the defaults the renders are unchanged.
group Detector and lookahead
Detector  "Detector"     0 1     0     enum Peak RMS                 | What every band's detector reads: the peak, or the RMS (3 ms mean square, on the peak scale: a sine reads the same as with Peak)
    how Chooses whether every band's detector reads the peak or the RMS level.
    sound Peak reacts quickly to hits; RMS is smoother and follows loudness more closely.
Lookahead "Lookahead"    0 1000  0     lin 0 10 ms 2                 | Delays the bands (and the dry) so each detector sees what is coming; adds this much latency to the phase's own, reported to NeoBuzz Live. A change fades the sound out and in over 10 ms each
    how Delays the bands by up to 10 ms so each detector sees what is coming.
    sound Fast peaks are caught cleanly, at the cost of extra latency.
group Band 1 upward and sidechain
B1UpRatio "B1 upward ratio" 0 1000 0 ratio 1 8              | Band 1: below the threshold the band is raised by (threshold - level) x (1 - 1/ratio), within Range, on the same knee and times (1:1 off; nothing is raised under -80 dBFS)
    how Raises band 1 when it falls below its threshold, up to 8:1 (1:1 is off).
    sound Quiet detail and tails in the band come up, giving a fuller, more even sound.
B1Key   "B1 sidechain" 0 1   0     enum Internal External          | Band 1: its detector hears the band's own signal, or input 2 through the same crossovers (connect a machine to the second input; none connected: it hears silence)
    how Chooses whether band 1's detector hears its own signal or the machine on the second input.
    sound External lets another sound, such as a kick, duck or lift this band.
group Band 2 upward and sidechain
B2UpRatio "B2 upward ratio" 0 1000 0 ratio 1 8              | Band 2: below the threshold the band is raised by (threshold - level) x (1 - 1/ratio), within Range, on the same knee and times (1:1 off; nothing is raised under -80 dBFS)
    how Raises band 2 when it falls below its threshold, up to 8:1 (1:1 is off).
    sound Quiet detail and tails in the band come up, giving a fuller, more even sound.
B2Key   "B2 sidechain" 0 1   0     enum Internal External          | Band 2: its detector hears the band's own signal, or input 2 through the same crossovers (connect a machine to the second input; none connected: it hears silence)
    how Chooses whether band 2's detector hears its own signal or the machine on the second input.
    sound External lets another sound, such as a kick, duck or lift this band.
group Band 3 upward and sidechain
B3UpRatio "B3 upward ratio" 0 1000 0 ratio 1 8              | Band 3: below the threshold the band is raised by (threshold - level) x (1 - 1/ratio), within Range, on the same knee and times (1:1 off; nothing is raised under -80 dBFS)
    how Raises band 3 when it falls below its threshold, up to 8:1 (1:1 is off).
    sound Quiet detail and tails in the band come up, giving a fuller, more even sound.
B3Key   "B3 sidechain" 0 1   0     enum Internal External          | Band 3: its detector hears the band's own signal, or input 2 through the same crossovers (connect a machine to the second input; none connected: it hears silence)
    how Chooses whether band 3's detector hears its own signal or the machine on the second input.
    sound External lets another sound, such as a kick, duck or lift this band.
group Band 4 upward and sidechain
B4UpRatio "B4 upward ratio" 0 1000 0 ratio 1 8              | Band 4: below the threshold the band is raised by (threshold - level) x (1 - 1/ratio), within Range, on the same knee and times (1:1 off; nothing is raised under -80 dBFS)
    how Raises band 4 when it falls below its threshold, up to 8:1 (1:1 is off).
    sound Quiet detail and tails in the band come up, giving a fuller, more even sound.
B4Key   "B4 sidechain" 0 1   0     enum Internal External          | Band 4: its detector hears the band's own signal, or input 2 through the same crossovers (connect a machine to the second input; none connected: it hears silence)
    how Chooses whether band 4's detector hears its own signal or the machine on the second input.
    sound External lets another sound, such as a kick, duck or lift this band.

# What the bands do (NeoMultibandMachine.Readings, machine_readings). Band 4's only with four bands.
reading b1_gr_db dB | Band 1's gain change now, as its meter shows it: positive cuts, negative boosts (upward expansion)
reading b1_gr_peak_db dB | Band 1's largest gain change over the last 3 s (positive cuts, negative boosts)
reading b1_level_db dBFS | Band 1's peak level over the last 3 s, as its detector reads it (set the threshold against it)
reading b2_gr_db dB | Band 2's gain change now, as its meter shows it: positive cuts, negative boosts (upward expansion)
reading b2_gr_peak_db dB | Band 2's largest gain change over the last 3 s (positive cuts, negative boosts)
reading b2_level_db dBFS | Band 2's peak level over the last 3 s, as its detector reads it (set the threshold against it)
reading b3_gr_db dB | Band 3's gain change now, as its meter shows it: positive cuts, negative boosts (upward expansion)
reading b3_gr_peak_db dB | Band 3's largest gain change over the last 3 s (positive cuts, negative boosts)
reading b3_level_db dBFS | Band 3's peak level over the last 3 s, as its detector reads it (set the threshold against it)
reading b4_gr_db dB | Band 4's gain change now, as its meter shows it: positive cuts, negative boosts (upward expansion)
reading b4_gr_peak_db dB | Band 4's largest gain change over the last 3 s (positive cuts, negative boosts)
reading b4_level_db dBFS | Band 4's peak level over the last 3 s, as its detector reads it (set the threshold against it)
reading bands | 3 or 4
reading latency_samples samples | The latency NeoBuzz Live compensates: 4607 at 44.1 and 48 kHz in linear phase, 0 in minimum phase
